    "result": "`invoice_totals` is implemented in `solution.py`. My 17 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't measure line coverage, so the 90% gate is unchecked. The tests exercise every branch I wrote, so I expect it to clear.\n\nThe function validates inputs and rounds each line's net and tax half-up to cents. It applies the bulk discount on top of the line discount for `standard` lines with qty 10 or more. It then builds the totals, the credit split and `tax_by_rate`, which includes a 0 rate when a line has one.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- empty invoices\n- credit that is smaller than and larger than the gross\n- the stacked 10% then 5% discount, which gives 85.50\n- per-line half-up rounding\n- region B rates\n- every `ValueError` case, including a `bool` qty\n- the 0 and 100 discount limits",
